ania deal? European leaders mock Donald Trump’s confused peace claims— Video</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/124280576.cms" /&gt;Former US President Donald Trump faced widespread amusement from world leaders, including Albanian PM Edi Rama and French President Emmanuel Macron, after repeatedly confusing Armenia with Albania. Trump boasted about brokering a peace deal in the South Caucasus, mistakenly claiming he settled a conflict involving Albania.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/azerbaijan-and-albania-deal-european-leaders-mock-donald-trumps-confused-peace-claims-video/articleshow/124280576.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/azerbaijan-and-albania-deal-european-leaders-mock-donald-trumps-confused-peace-claims-video/articleshow/124280576.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-10-03T06:12:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-124280688,imgsize-36062.cms"/></item><item><title>‘Disgusting atrocity’: Vladimir Putin condemns Charlie Kirk’s assassination; cites ‘deep rift’ in American society</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/124280653.cms" /&gt;Russian President Vladimir Putin condemned the assassination of conservative activist Charlie Kirk as a "disgusting crime" and offered condolences, noting the live broadcast. He linked the killing to a "deep rift" in American society, while also pushing back against Trump's "paper tiger" characterization of Russia's military efforts in Ukraine.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/disgusting-atrocity-vladimir-putin-condemns-charlie-kirks-assassination-cites-deep-rift-in-american-society/articleshow/124280653.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/disgusting-atrocity-vladimir-putin-condemns-charlie-kirks-assassination-cites-deep-rift-in-american-society/articleshow/124280653.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-10-03T06:02:08+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-124280656,imgsize-539471.cms"/></item><item><title>US government shutdown: Education dept employees' out-of-office emails altered to blame Democrats; claim 'none of us contested'</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/124280514.cms" /&gt;Furloughed Education Department employees discovered their out-of-office emails were manipulated to include partisan messages blaming Democrats for the government shutdown. Civil servants, fearing Hatch Act violations, reported these unauthorized changes, which a department official defended. They expressed frustration over being forced to convey political statements.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-government-shutdown-education-dept-employees-out-of-office-emails-altered-to-blame-democrats-claim-none-of-us-contested/articleshow/124280514.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-government-shutdown-education-dept-employees-out-of-office-emails-altered-to-blame-democrats-claim-none-of-us-contested/articleshow/124280514.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-10-03T05:36:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-124280571,imgsize-59156.cms"/></item><item><title>Manchester synagogue stabbing: UK Police name suspected attacker; who is Syrian-origin man Jihad Al-Shamie?</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin